{{Quote|The droid was sent to Vassek based on intel from a captured smuggler. It scanned a settlement on the planet for six weeks, recording conversations between local farmers.|Viper 058-V-2353's report|<ref name="Outlaws" />}}
'''Vassek''' was a terrestrial [[planet]] located in the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim's]] [[Wazta sector]], within the [[Vassek system]]. It had three [[moon]]s&mdash;one of which was [[Vassek 3]]. Vassek was relatively obscure by the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]], though became less so following a [[Mission to Grievous's castle|confrontation]] between the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[General]] [[Grievous]] and a [[Galactic Republic]] [[task force]] on Vassek 3. During the [[Imperial Era]], the Vassek [[farmer]] [[Roni]] made plans to [[Thief|steal]] [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] generators. After [[viper probe droid]] [[Viper 058-V-2353]]'s [[Investigation on Vassek|investigations]] on the world uncovered their plot, the farmer and two of their family members were arrested by an [[Unidentified Imperial Security Bureau agent (Vassek)|Imperial Security Bureau agent]], and a report of the [[probe droid]]'s endeavors was kept on a [[datapad]].

==Description==
The terrestrial [[planet]] Vassek<ref name="Outlaws" /> was located in the [[Wazta sector]]'s [[Vassek system]], at [[Standard Galactic Grid]] square I-17. A small [[Color|blue]]-and-green planet, it was one of many in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] that was named and noted, but<ref name="BMF 65" /> whose obscurity<ref name="HC 64">{{HelmetCollectionCite|64|Databank A-Z}}</ref> and distance from the [[Koda Spur]] [[hyperspace route]] made it uninteresting to [[the galaxy]]. Vassek and those other Outer Rim planets offered no uncommonly found resources that could not be obtained easier elsewhere. The world was [[orbit]]ed by three [[moon]]s, one of which was [[Vassek 3]].<ref name="BMF 65" />

==History==
{{Quote|A farmer named Roni expressed actionable plans to steal Imperial generators. An ISB agent was deployed and captured the suspect along with two adult members of the family.|Viper 058-V-2353's Vassek investigation report|<ref name="Outlaws" />}}
[[File:SaberTruthCover.png|thumb|right|270px|Grievous had a personal fortress on the moon of Vassek.]]
By the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], Vassek's moon&mdash;Vassek 3&mdash;was home to Separatist [[General]] [[Grievous]]'s [[Grievous's fortress|personal fortress]].<ref name="LoG">{{TCW|Lair of Grievous}}</ref> In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> during the Clone Wars, a Republic [[task force]] traveled to Vassek 3 in search of the [[Rescue on the Tranquility|escaped]] [[Viceroy of the Trade Federation|Viceroy]] [[Nute Gunray]].<ref name="LoG" /> Following<ref name="HC 64" /> the Republic's [[Mission to Grievous's castle|confrontation]] with Grievous,<ref name="LoG" /> Vassek became less obscure.<ref name="HC 64" />

During the [[Imperial Era]], the [[farmer]] [[Roni]] and their [[Roni's family|family]] lived on Vassek.<ref name="Outlaws" /> At some point by [[3 ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> the farmer made plans to [[Thief|steal]] generators from the [[Galactic Empire]]; around the same time, a [[Unidentified smuggler (Roni)|smuggler]] learned of the anti-Imperial sentiment on Vassek. Upon being captured by the Empire, the [[smuggler]] gave up their intel on Vassek, prompting the former to send the [[viper probe droid]] [[Viper 058-V-2353]] to [[Investigation on Vassek|investigate]]. While on the world, the [[probe droid]] conducted surveillance on the local populace by spending six [[Standard week|weeks]] recording conversations between farmers in a Vassek [[Unidentified settlement (Vassek)|settlement]]. When Viper 058-V-2353 discovered Roni's plans to steal generators, an [[Unidentified Imperial Security Bureau agent (Vassek)|agent]] of the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] was dispatched to Vassek and arrested the farmer and two adult members of their family. After the endeavor, the probe [[droid]] left Vassek and returned to the Empire's [[Derosha Six]] [[space station]], where a report of its investigation on the world was stored on a [[datapad]].<ref name="Outlaws" />

{{GameMechanics|Star Wars Outlaws}}
In 3 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate" /> the outlaw [[Kay Vess]] [[Infiltration of Derosha Six|infiltrated]] Derosha Six and read the datapad mentioning Vassek while evading Imperial personnel.<ref name="Outlaws" />
{{EndGame}}

==Inhabitants==
During the Empire's reign, Vassek was home to a number of farmers.<ref name="Outlaws" />

==Locations==
By 3 ABY,<ref name="OutlawsDate" /> a settlement was established on Vassek.<ref name="Outlaws" />

==Behind the scenes==
Vassek first appeared in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in "[[Lair of Grievous]],"<ref name="LoG" /> the tenth episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', which aired on [[December 12]], [[2008]]. The planet was identified in the corresponding episode guide on [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="Lair of Grievous Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode010.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Lair of Grievous}}</ref> The [[Planet/Legends|planet]] [[Vassek/Legends|Vassek]] originally appeared in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity in "[[The Clone Wars: The Dreams of General Grievous]],"<ref name="The Dreams of Grievous">"[[The Clone Wars: The Dreams of General Grievous]]"</ref> a [[Star Wars comic books|webcomic]] in the [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (webcomics)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' webcomic series]] authored by [[Pablo Hidalgo]]<ref name="The Clone Wars online comic 77">{{SWArchive|url=clonewars/comic/?book=season1#/?page=77|text=''The Clone Wars'' webcomic (p.77)|nobackup=1}}</ref> and published on [[December 10]], 2008.<ref name="The Clone Wars archives-ninth page">{{SWArchive|url=archives/index.html?c=d6de5d83-4da5-48ab-bf34-75cd3af8fbef&k=&page=7|text=''The Clone Wars'' archives-seventh page}}</ref>

[[File:Rodia_canon.png|thumb|right|250px|Vassek was illustrated using a version of a piece of artwork also depicting other worlds, such as Rodia (pictured).]]
The depiction of Vassek in "Lair of Grievous" utilized a recolored version<ref name="LoG" /> of artwork used to depict several unidentified celestial bodies in ''[[Fierce Twilight]]'',<ref name="FierceTwilight">{{CN|url=tv_shows/starwars/games/game_01_ext.html|text=''Fierce Twilight''|int=Fierce Twilight}}</ref> a [[September 3]], 2008<ref name="FierceTwilightDate">{{CN|url=games/index.html|text=Cartoon Network Games Homepage|oldversion=20080903105905}}</ref> ''Star Wars'' Legends web browser game published on the official [[Cartoon Network]] website.<ref name="FierceTwilight" /> The artwork from ''Fierce Twilight'' was also used to illustrate<ref name="BombadJedi">{{TCW|Bombad Jedi}}</ref> the planet [[Rodia]]<ref name="TVE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> beginning with "[[Bombad Jedi]],"<ref name="BombadJedi" /> the eighth episode of ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars''{{'s}} first season that first aired on [[November 21]], 2008,<ref name="Episode Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Episode Guide]]''</ref> as well as the planet [[Teth]]<ref name="TVE" />&mdash;in [[2010]] in Legends<ref name="TCWOfficialEpGuideSeries12">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars Official Episode Guide Series 1 & 2]]''</ref> and from [[2017]]<ref name="TVE" /> onward in the current canon.<ref name="Battles">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref> In addition, a version of that same image sharing its color palette with the depiction of Vassek was used to illustrate the cover of "[[Republic and Separatist Ships (1)]],"<ref name="Separatist Ships">{{EncyclopediaCite|Republic and Separatist Ships (1)}}</ref> a [[November 2]], [[2021]],<ref name="De Agostini">{{DeAgostini|url=libros-comics/enciclopedia-star-wars|text=Star Wars Encyclopedia}}</ref> booklet of [[De Agostini]]'s [[Star Wars Encyclopedia (series)|''Star Wars Encyclopedia'']] series. However, this articles refrains from assuming that the illustration depicts Vassek.<ref name="Separatist Ships" />

